{n:2,t:"Which is the binary fraction nearest equivalent to the decimal fraction 23.375?",o:["10111.011","10111.110","11101.011","11101.110"],a:0,e:["Correct: 23 = 16 + 4 + 2 + 1 = 10111. The fraction 0.375 = 0.25 + 0.125 = .011 in binary. Together: 10111.011.","Wrong: The integer part 10111 is right, but .110 = 0.5 + 0.25 = 0.75, not 0.375.","Wrong: 11101 = 29, not 23, so the integer part is wrong.","Wrong: 11101 = 29 and .110 = 0.75, so both parts are wrong."]},
{n:9,t:"Which term is used for the special CPU register used by push and pop instructions?",o:["Instruction register","Program counter","Stack pointer","Status register"],a:2,e:["Wrong: The instruction register holds the instruction currently being decoded.","Wrong: The program counter holds the address of the next instruction to fetch.","Correct: The stack pointer holds the address of the top of the stack. Push and pop move it up or down as data is added or removed.","Wrong: The status (flag) register holds condition flags such as zero, carry and overflow."]},
{n:16,t:"Which is an appropriate explanation of an actuator?",o:["It amplifies weak electrical signals from microphones, sensors and similar devices","It compares a target value with a controlled value from a sensor and outputs an operation amount","It converts power from an energy source into rotation, translational motion or other movements based on control signals","It detects position, angle, velocity, temperature and similar parameters and converts them into electrical information"],a:2,e:["Wrong: That describes an amplifier.","Wrong: That describes a controller, which closes the feedback loop between target and measured value.","Correct: An actuator, such as a motor or cylinder, turns energy into physical movement when it receives a control signal.","Wrong: That describes a sensor, which is the input side, whereas an actuator is the output side."]},
{n:18,t:"Of the functions provided by a DBMS, which is a means for protecting data confidentiality?",o:["Checking referential constraints when data is updated","Managing a transaction that combines a series of processes as a logical unit","Managing the data access rights of users","Placing an exclusive lock on data before updates"],a:2,e:["Wrong: Referential constraints protect integrity, so that foreign keys point to existing rows.","Wrong: Transactions protect consistency and atomicity.","Correct: Granting and revoking rights such as SELECT, UPDATE and DELETE per user stops unauthorized people from reading data, which is confidentiality.","Wrong: Exclusive locks prevent concurrent update conflicts, which concerns integrity and isolation."]},
{n:24,t:"In the OSI model, which layer is responsible for routing datagrams between hosts using IP addresses across one or more networks?",o:["Data link","Network","Physical","Transport"],a:1,e:["Wrong: The data link layer moves frames within one link using MAC addresses.","Correct: The network layer (layer 3) handles IP addressing and routing between networks.","Wrong: The physical layer deals with signals, cables and connectors.","Wrong: The transport layer (TCP/UDP) provides end-to-end delivery between processes using ports."]},
{n:32,t:"Which is the function of a WAF?",o:["Encrypting data and controlling access on a web server","Inspecting and filtering HTTP requests","Managing user authentication and authorization","Scanning malware on a web server"],a:1,e:["Wrong: Encryption is done by TLS and access control by the server or OS.","Correct: A Web Application Firewall inspects HTTP/HTTPS traffic and blocks attacks such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting.","Wrong: Authentication and authorization belong to the application or an identity system.","Wrong: Malware scanning is the job of antivirus software."]},
{n:38,t:"Which test ensures that the interfaces and linkages between different parts of software work properly?",o:["Functional test","Integration test","Performance test","Unit test"],a:1,e:["Wrong: A functional test checks that features meet their specifications.","Correct: Integration testing combines modules and checks the interfaces and data passing between them.","Wrong: A performance test measures speed, load and response time.","Wrong: A unit test checks a single module in isolation."]},
{n:40,t:"Which is an appropriate explanation of a Sprint in Scrum?",o:["A daily meeting where members review progress and plan the day’s work","A fixed-length period dedicated to developing a product increment","A self-organizing team responsible for product development","A list of tasks and features the Scrum team has yet to complete"],a:1,e:["Wrong: That is the Daily Scrum.","Correct: A Sprint is a time-boxed iteration, usually 1–4 weeks, that produces a potentially releasable increment.","Wrong: That is the Scrum Team.","Wrong: That is the Product Backlog."]},
{n:44,t:"Which relation should be accomplished in service management concerning MTD, RPO and RTO?",o:["MTD < RPO","MTD < RTO","RPO < MTD","RTO < MTD"],a:3,e:["Wrong: RPO is about acceptable data loss in time, not a downtime limit, so it is not compared this way.","Wrong: If MTD were smaller than RTO, recovery would take longer than the business can tolerate.","Wrong: RPO and MTD measure different things, so this comparison is not the required relation.","Correct: Recovery (RTO) must finish within the maximum tolerable downtime (MTD), so RTO < MTD."]},
{n:52,t:"Which is an explanation of Supply Chain Management (SCM)?",o:["Customer information from various channels is consolidated to build closer relationships","Employees’ skills are grasped for appropriate personnel assignment and evaluation","Individuals’ know-how is shared across the organization","Business operations from purchasing and production to sales and distribution are reexamined for total optimization, shortening delivery times and minimizing inventory"],a:3,e:["Wrong: That is CRM.","Wrong: That is human resources or talent management.","Wrong: That is knowledge management.","Correct: SCM optimizes the whole flow from procurement to delivery across and between companies."]},
{n:59,t:"Which is an appropriate explanation of Process mining?",o:["A management strategy to change workflows by emphasizing new ideas","A method of analyzing data sets and finding unsuspected relationships","A methodology for improving performance by removing unnecessary data","A technique for analyzing and improving business processes using knowledge extracted from event logs"],a:3,e:["Wrong: That resembles business process reengineering.","Wrong: That describes data mining, which the question contrasts with process mining.","Wrong: Removing unnecessary data is not process mining.","Correct: Process mining reconstructs how processes actually run from system event logs, then finds bottlenecks and deviations."]}
];
